## Sensing Architecture: Two Modalities

BLIND MODALITY (proprioception + F/T):
- Arm joint encoders → forward kinematics → door angle θ(t)
  θ(t) = atan2(p_y - h_y, p_x - h_x)
  where p = handle position, h = hinge position, both from FK
- Wrist F/T → hinge torque: τ = (r × F)·ẑ
- Both feed RLS → [Î, μ̂] updated online
- Used during contact/manipulation phase

VISION MODALITY (not yet built):
- Camera → point cloud → kinematic model estimation (hinge axis, position)
- Appearance-based inertia prior (coarse visual guess fed as weak prior)
- Used before and during grasp for approach planning
- Replaces hardcoded geometry in current simulation

The two modalities are complementary: vision covers pre-grasp kinematics, 
blind modality covers in-contact inertial estimation.

