## Scope Decisions Made

- Revolute joints only for inertial estimation (prismatic collapses to 
  trivial F=ma, one-parameter problem — not comparably interesting)
- Kinematic formulation stays joint-type-agnostic via screw theory
- Multi-joint extension is architecturally possible (regressor generalizes 
  to τ = Φ(q,q̇,q̈)·π via classical Atkeson 1986 result — still linear 
  in parameters) but thesis-scale, not ICRA-scale
- Vision-only inertial estimation is impossible for vertical-hinge doors 
  (gravity torque = 0, applied torque unknown → underdetermined) — this 
  is an identifiability result, not a current-methods limitation
- Dedicated wrist F/T sensor can be replaced by arm's own joint torque 
  sensing (KUKA iiwa 14 has this natively) — reduces hardware requirements

